        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Fluid dynamics describes the motion of liquids and gases. It is one of the oldest and richest fields of applied mathematics, and it contains some of the deepest unsolved problems in science — most famously, the Clay Millennium Prize for the Navier-Stokes existence and smoothness problem. Reynolds number is the single most important dimensionless parameter in the field: it separates laminar from turbulent flow, simple from complex behavior, analytically tractable from computationally intractable."
    },
